      "blocks": {
        "q9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "tech pack",
            "title": "is the first tech pack really free?",
            "body": "yes. add an image and your email at hub.thefuturebasics.com/start and the assistant drafts your first tech pack at no cost, no card needed. after that it is $48 a pack, or $100 a month for unlimited packs on the studio membership. see every plan at hub.thefuturebasics.com/pricing."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "plan",
            "title": "what do i get for $48?",
            "body": "an assistant draft from your image with callouts, measurements, materials, construction and colourways, a cost estimate you can edit, then a review by future basics, a published version 1, a factory version in chinese (simplified or traditional), spanish, portuguese or italian, and an excel or pdf download. you can edit it any time."
          }
        },
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "minimums",
            "title": "what is the real minimum?",
            "body": "fifty pieces on most items, apparel included. plush is three hundred. toys depend on tooling. footwear and electronics are a different scale entirely, and we say so upfront rather than let you find out later."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "production",
            "title": "what does production cost?",
            "body": "the tools are priced above: $499 for 90 days of the design lab, $100 a month for the membership, or $48 a pack. production is quoted per style from your tech pack and billed at transparent landed cost. you see the invoice."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "audience",
            "title": "do i need a certain audience size?",
            "body": "no. a forty-thousand-person email list that opens is worth more here than a million passive followers."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "first time",
            "title": "do i need to have sold merch before?",
            "body": "no. plenty of the best projects are someone's first product."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "companies",
            "title": "do you work with companies as well as creators?",
            "body": "equally. roughly half this business is brands who want product worth paying for rather than swag worth throwing out."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "timing",
            "title": "how long does it take?",
            "body": "ten to fourteen weeks for apparel, design to delivery. ten to sixteen for plush. footwear and electronics run six to twelve months."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "risk",
            "title": "what if it does not sell?",
            "body": "we will tell you before we make it if we think the product is wrong. and at fifty pieces, being wrong is survivable — that is rather the point of the minimum."
          }
        },
        "q11": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "software",
            "title": "do you build software for other businesses?",
            "body": "yes. the hub on this page is ours, and we build the same kind of tooling for brands: client portals, approval workflows, ai that turns images and documents into structured work, payments and partner networks. tell us what is slowing the business down and we will scope it, usually from four weeks."
          }
        },
        "q12": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "excel",
            "title": "can i open it in excel?",
            "body": "yes. every pack downloads as one excel workbook with a sheet each for materials, measurements, colourways, skus and cost, or as csv for any single sheet. the version a factory gets leaves out your retail price and your costs."
          }
        },
        "q13": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "costs",
            "title": "is the cost estimate a quote?",
            "body": "no. it is your own arithmetic: a unit cost on each material, plus labour, decoration, packaging, freight and duty, added up to a landed cost and a margin, with price breaks at the order sizes you choose. a factory's quote replaces it, and factories never see it."
          }
        },
        "q14": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "design lab",
            "title": "what is the design lab?",
            "body": "the studio we design with, open in your own room. six ways in: describe it, pick it from the recipe menu, start from one of 382 flat sketches, draw it from scratch, plan a whole line, or bring a photo. it covers clothes, headwear, bags, footwear, plush, toys and electronics, and every way ends in a tech pack."
          }
        },
        "q15": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "designer",
            "title": "do i need to be a designer?",
            "body": "no. the recipe menu is made for people who are not: pick a base, add the details, choose a colour system, and the flats are drawn for you. designers get the pro tools in the same place."
          }
        },
        "q16": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "lab price",
            "title": "what does $499 get me?",
            "body": "the design lab in your own room for 90 days, with 40 ai generations included and $2.50 each after that. tech packs are included while it is open."
          }
        },
        "q17": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "key": "edit",
            "title": "can i change what the recipe draws?",
            "body": "yes. every pocket, zip and collar it places is a detail you can move, resize, recolour or delete in the studio, and edit recipe reopens the menu with your picks."
          }
        }
      },
